*`chert-quay`** (C-94c506a3 — truncated SQLite salvage): The agent must decode the SQLite header (page size, header page count), classify truncation mode (`intact` / `page_aligned` / `mid_page`), and salvage readable rows via zero-pad-to-header-size + read-only rowid probing (which correctly recovers cells of a partial page that lie within surviving bytes, while losing the rest). Deliverables: `/app/solve.py` + `/app/salvaged.json`; verifier executes the program on the visible DB plus 4 hidden DBs covering all three modes.

2. **`mist-buoy`** (C-15878c3b — contract discovery from hosted schema doc): A live tide-gauge archive API serves its full contract only at `GET /contract.json` (auth header+key, `/api/v2/` prefix, cursor pagination, 202-then-poll async reports, campaign constants). The agent writes `/app/client.py` that reads the doc then follows it, producing `/app/report.json`. Hidden instances run the same server with different data files (different contract version, archive key, select status, metric, window, page counts, incl. a zero-reading null-stat case), so every hard-coded value fails.

Both are deterministic, stdlib-only, no network beyond localhost at verify time, verifier timeouts ≤ 300s, and `lint_tasks.py` reports no problems for either task (27 remaining problems pre-exist in other tasks).

